{
  "hosting": {
    "public": "frontend/build",
    "$comment_ignore": "The dotfile glob is spelled out rather than '**/.*': the Claude Code plugin (§R3) keeps its manifest in /lib/claude-plugin/.claude-plugin/, and a blanket '**/.*' would silently drop it from the deploy. frontend/build is generated, so the only dot-entries that can appear there are the ones listed here.",
    "ignore": [
      "firebase.json",
      "**/.DS_Store",
      "**/.git/**",
      "**/.gitignore",
      "**/.firebase/**",
      "**/.env*",
      "**/node_modules/**"
    ],
    "rewrites": [
      {
        "source": "/oauth/consent",
        "destination": "/index.html"
      },
      {
        "source": "/api/**",
        "function": {
          "functionId": "api",
          "region": "us-central1"
        }
      },
      {
        "source": "/v1/**",
        "function": {
          "functionId": "api",
          "region": "us-central1"
        }
      },
      {
        "source": "/mcp",
        "function": {
          "functionId": "api",
          "region": "us-central1"
        }
      },
      {
        "source": "/mcp/**",
        "function": {
          "functionId": "api",
          "region": "us-central1"
        }
      },
      {
        "source": "/oauth/**",
        "function": {
          "functionId": "api",
          "region": "us-central1"
        }
      },
      {
        "source": "/hooks/**",
        "function": {
          "functionId": "api",
          "region": "us-central1"
        }
      },
      {
        "source": "/ics/**",
        "function": {
          "functionId": "api",
          "region": "us-central1"
        }
      },
      {
        "source": "/integrations/**",
        "function": {
          "functionId": "api",
          "region": "us-central1"
        }
      },
      {
        "source": "/.well-known/**",
        "function": {
          "functionId": "api",
          "region": "us-central1"
        }
      },
      {
        "source": "**",
        "destination": "/index.html"
      }
    ],
    "$comment_headers": "The hosted SDK, /lib/** (docs/plan/agents.html §M). Hosting applies EVERY matching block, later ones winning a header the earlier ones also set — so the wide rules come first and the specific ones last. scripts/deploy-lib.mjs stages the files; scripts/deploy-lib-check.mjs asserts these headers against a running hosting emulator.",
    "headers": [
      {
        "comment": "Anything under /lib is meant to be fetched cross-origin: a browser <script type=module>, a Deno URL import, an npm tarball URL.",
        "source": "/lib/**",
        "headers": [
          { "key": "Access-Control-Allow-Origin", "value": "*" },
          { "key": "Access-Control-Allow-Methods", "value": "GET, HEAD, OPTIONS" },
          { "key": "Access-Control-Allow-Headers", "value": "*" },
          { "key": "Access-Control-Expose-Headers", "value": "X-TypeScript-Types, Content-Length, Content-Type" },
          { "key": "Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy", "value": "cross-origin" },
          { "key": "X-Content-Type-Options", "value": "nosniff" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "comment": "Content types hosting would otherwise guess wrong: .ts is NOT video/mp2t here, and a .tgz served as octet-stream makes npm's download path fussy. .d.ts ends in .ts, so one rule covers both.",
        "source": "/lib/**/*.ts",
        "headers": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/typescript; charset=utf-8" }]
      },
      {
        "source": "/lib/**/*.js",
        "headers": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "text/javascript; charset=utf-8" }]
      },
      {
        "source": "/lib/**/*.tgz",
        "headers": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/gzip" }]
      },
      {
        "source": "/lib/**/*.json",
        "headers": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }]
      },
      {
        "comment": "The Claude plugin (§R3) is served as a browsable folder as well as a zip: hosting guesses nothing useful for .md, and a plugin bundle downloaded as octet-stream confuses the browser's Save dialog.",
        "source": "/lib/**/*.md",
        "headers": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "text/markdown; charset=utf-8" }]
      },
      {
        "source": "/lib/**/*.zip",
        "headers": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/zip" }]
      },
      {
        "comment": "Pinned: the files under /lib/v1 are what a consumer's lockfile and an editor's cache point at, so they are immutable for a year.",
        "source": "/lib/v1/**",
        "headers": [{ "key": "Cache-Control", "value": "public, max-age=31536000, immutable" }]
      },
      {
        "comment": "The moving name: always the newest build, so nothing may keep a copy.",
        "source": "/lib/latest/**",
        "headers": [{ "key": "Cache-Control", "value": "no-store" }]
      },
      {
        "comment": "The install page changes with the docs; revalidate it every time. A header rule is matched against the REQUEST PATH, not the file hosting resolves it to, and a trailing slash is normalised away — so /lib/ needs the '/lib' spelling and only a direct hit needs '/lib/index.html'.",
        "source": "/lib",
        "headers": [{ "key": "Cache-Control", "value": "no-cache" }]
      },
      {
        "source": "/lib/",
        "headers": [{ "key": "Cache-Control", "value": "no-cache" }]
      },
      {
        "source": "/lib/index.html",
        "headers": [{ "key": "Cache-Control", "value": "no-cache" }]
      },
      {
        "comment": "The plugin moves with every release and carries the whole integration context inside it, so a cached copy is a copy that describes an older API. Revalidate, never store.",
        "source": "/lib/claude-plugin.zip",
        "headers": [{ "key": "Cache-Control", "value": "no-cache" }]
      },
      {
        "source": "/lib/claude-plugin/**",
        "headers": [{ "key": "Cache-Control", "value": "no-cache" }]
      },
      {
        "comment": "A URL import only carries types if the server says where they are. Deno reads this header (and the triple-slash reference the bundle starts with); an absolute path so it resolves the same from any importing module. sdk*.js is sdk.js and sdk.min.js.",
        "source": "/lib/v1/sdk*.js",
        "headers": [{ "key": "X-TypeScript-Types", "value": "/lib/v1/sdk.d.ts" }]
      },
      {
        "source": "/lib/latest/sdk*.js",
        "headers": [{ "key": "X-TypeScript-Types", "value": "/lib/latest/sdk.d.ts" }]
      },
      {
        "comment": "The integration context an orchestrator is pointed at (docs/plan/agents.html §O). Generated by scripts/gen-integration.mjs; scripts/deploy-lib-check.mjs asserts these headers against a running hosting emulator. An agent fetches these from anywhere, so CORS is open, and they are NEVER cached: an agent that re-reads the page is asking whether its knowledge is current, and a cached answer would defeat the question. The charset is explicit so a fetch cannot guess latin-1 on the em dashes.",
        "source": "/llms*.txt",
        "headers": [
          { "key": "Access-Control-Allow-Origin", "value": "*" },
          { "key": "Access-Control-Allow-Methods", "value": "GET, HEAD, OPTIONS" },
          { "key": "Access-Control-Allow-Headers", "value": "*" },
          { "key": "Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy", "value": "cross-origin" },
          { "key": "X-Content-Type-Options", "value": "nosniff" },
          { "key": "Cache-Control", "value": "no-store" },
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "text/plain; charset=utf-8" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "source": "/integrate.json",
        "headers": [
          { "key": "Access-Control-Allow-Origin", "value": "*" },
          { "key": "Access-Control-Allow-Methods", "value": "GET, HEAD, OPTIONS" },
          { "key": "Access-Control-Allow-Headers", "value": "*" },
          { "key": "Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy", "value": "cross-origin" },
          { "key": "X-Content-Type-Options", "value": "nosniff" },
          { "key": "Cache-Control", "value": "no-store" },
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "comment": "The readable page. Three spellings because a header rule matches the REQUEST path: what people type, the normalised directory, and the file itself.",
        "source": "/integrate",
        "headers": [
          { "key": "Access-Control-Allow-Origin", "value": "*" },
          { "key": "Cache-Control", "value": "no-cache" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "source": "/integrate/",
        "headers": [
          { "key": "Access-Control-Allow-Origin", "value": "*" },
          { "key": "Cache-Control", "value": "no-cache" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "source": "/integrate/index.html",
        "headers": [
          { "key": "Access-Control-Allow-Origin", "value": "*" },
          { "key": "Cache-Control", "value": "no-cache" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "comment": "The Claude setup guide (§R3) — the same three spellings, for the same reason.",
        "source": "/integrate/claude",
        "headers": [
          { "key": "Access-Control-Allow-Origin", "value": "*" },
          { "key": "Cache-Control", "value": "no-cache" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "source": "/integrate/claude/",
        "headers": [
          { "key": "Access-Control-Allow-Origin", "value": "*" },
          { "key": "Cache-Control", "value": "no-cache" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "source": "/integrate/claude/index.html",
        "headers": [
          { "key": "Access-Control-Allow-Origin", "value": "*" },
          { "key": "Cache-Control", "value": "no-cache" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "comment": "THE PWA (docs/plan/agents.html \u00a7S). None of these carry a content hash, so hosting's default hour of caching would decide how long a phone keeps the old app: a service worker that is not revalidated is a deploy nobody receives. 'no-cache' means revalidate, not 'do not store' \u2014 a 304 is still cheap. Service-Worker-Allowed is belt and braces for the '/' scope.",
        "source": "/service-worker.js",
        "headers": [
          { "key": "Cache-Control", "value": "no-cache" },
          { "key": "Service-Worker-Allowed", "value": "/" },
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "text/javascript; charset=utf-8" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "source": "/firebase-messaging-sw.js",
        "headers": [
          { "key": "Cache-Control", "value": "no-cache" },
          { "key": "Service-Worker-Allowed", "value": "/" },
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "text/javascript; charset=utf-8" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "comment": "Hosting would otherwise guess .webmanifest wrong; a browser that does not see a manifest type will not offer to install.",
        "source": "/manifest.webmanifest",
        "headers": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/manifest+json; charset=utf-8" },
          { "key": "Cache-Control", "value": "no-cache" }
        ]
      },
      {
        "source": "/offline.html",
        "headers": [{ "key": "Cache-Control", "value": "no-cache" }]
      }
    ],
    "predeploy": [
      "node \"$PROJECT_DIR/scripts/deploy-guard.mjs\""
    ]
  },
  "functions": [
    {
      "source": "backend",
      "codebase": "default",
      "runtime": "nodejs22",
      "ignore": [
        "node_modules",
        ".git",
        "test",
        "src",
        "*.log",
        "firebase-debug.log"
      ],
      "predeploy": [
        "node \"$PROJECT_DIR/scripts/deploy-guard.mjs\""
      ]
    }
  ],
  "firestore": {
    "rules": "backend/firestore.rules",
    "indexes": "backend/firestore.indexes.json"
  },
  "storage": {
    "rules": "backend/storage.rules"
  },
  "database": {
    "rules": "backend/database.rules.json"
  },
  "emulators": {
    "auth": {
      "host": "127.0.0.1",
      "port": 9209
    },
    "firestore": {
      "host": "127.0.0.1",
      "port": 8380,
      "websocketPort": 9350
    },
    "database": {
      "host": "127.0.0.1",
      "port": 9300
    },
    "storage": {
      "host": "127.0.0.1",
      "port": 9309
    },
    "functions": {
      "host": "127.0.0.1",
      "port": 5101
    },
    "hosting": {
      "host": "127.0.0.1",
      "port": 5050
    },
    "tasks": {
      "host": "127.0.0.1",
      "port": 9599
    },
    "eventarc": {
      "host": "127.0.0.1",
      "port": 9699
    },
    "hub": {
      "host": "127.0.0.1",
      "port": 4411
    },
    "logging": {
      "host": "127.0.0.1",
      "port": 4412
    },
    "ui": {
      "enabled": true,
      "host": "127.0.0.1",
      "port": 4410
    },
    "singleProjectMode": true
  }
}
